World Bank World Development Indicators
---------------------------------------

Datasets: currency_fx, currency_deflator, and the Currency rates in
          convert_data

Series:   PA.NUS.FCRF     official exchange rate, LCU per US$, period average
          NY.GDP.DEFL.ZS  GDP deflator
          FP.CPI.TOTL     consumer price index

Attribution: The World Bank: World Development Indicators

Licence:  Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 International (CC BY 4.0)
          https://datacatalog.worldbank.org/public-licenses
          https://data.worldbank.org/summary-terms-of-use

Note:     PA.NUS.FCRF credits IMF International Financial Statistics as its
          own source.

Changes:  The series are not shipped as published. CC BY 4.0 asks that
          changes be stated, so:
            * rows are re-keyed from country and year to CURRENCY and year,
              with one row per currency union rather than per member;
            * the numeraire's own rows are synthesised, since a US dollar is
              one US dollar in every year by definition rather than by
              measurement (they carry source = "numeraire");
            * a currency with no deflator of its own takes one from a member
              economy, named in currency_deflator$area -- the euro deflates
              on Germany, there being no euro-area series;
            * a year with no value, or a non-positive one, is dropped rather
              than interpolated or carried forward;
            * the Currency rates in convert_data are derived from
              currency_fx at one base year, as its reciprocal (US dollars
              per unit, where the series publishes units per US dollar).
          data-raw/currency.R is the whole derivation, and nothing else
          touches the values.

